From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dpnet: IDirectPlay8ThreadPool thread counts, DoWork and thread messages

The thread pool is a process wide service: GetThreadCount / SetThreadCount
now keep the count (processor -1 for the total, or one processor number
below 64, INVALIDPARAM above), SetThreadCount sends DPN_MSGID_CREATE_THREAD /
DPN_MSGID_DESTROY_THREAD to the registered handler for each thread added or
removed, DoWork answers NOTREADY while the pool has threads (and UNINITIALIZED
or INVALIDFLAGS as usual), Close resets the counts. No worker threads are
started. The todo_wine marks of thread.c that now pass are removed.

